I am sitting in the U-Bahn and riding across the city.
The small box from the bakery rests safely on my lap.
I must not put it in my backpack.
The dessert has to stay completely flat.
I take out my phone with one hand.
I write Nele a short message.
I write to her that I will arrive in ten minutes.
Afterwards I quickly put the phone away again.
The journey does not take much longer.
The U-Bahn stops at the station and I get off.
I walk up the stairs and come outside.
It is a very mild spring evening.
The sky is still bright and the weather is pleasant.
I only have to walk a few more streets.
I carry the box carefully with both hands again.
The new neighborhood looks very nice.
I hope that the dessert will taste good to Nele.
Soon I will be standing at her door.
